  setActiveConversationId(null);
}, []);
```

Sets `activeConversationId` to `null`, indicating no conversation is selected.

---

## 2. MESSAGE SENDING (Triggering Conversation Creation)

### ChatInput Component
**File:** `/Users/cyyeh/Desktop/duckdb-data-agent/.claude/worktrees/implement-memory/frontend/src/components/ChatInput.tsx` (lines 47-62)

When the user sends a message:

```typescript
const handleSend = async () => {
  const trimmed = text.trim();
  if (!trimmed || isStreaming) return;
  setText('');
  setShowSlashMenu(false);

  let convId = activeConversationId;
  if (!convId) {
    convId = await createConversation(trimmed);  // Create conversation here
  }
  await sendMessage(trimmed, convId);  // Send message with conversation ID
  triggerRefresh();
};
```

**Key Logic:**
- If `activeConversationId` is `null`, the app calls `createConversation(trimmed)` using the first message as the title
- The new conversation ID is returned and used for `sendMessage()`

### Conversation Creation API Call
**File:** `/Users/cyyeh/Desktop/duckdb-data-agent/.claude/worktrees/implement-memory/frontend/src/contexts/ConversationContext.tsx` (lines 40-51)

```typescript
const createConversation = useCallback(async (firstMessage: string): Promise<string> => {
  const title = firstMessage.length > 50 ? firstMessage.slice(0, 50) + '...' : firstMessage;
  const res = await fetch('/api/conversations', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'X-Session-ID': sessionId },
    body: JSON.stringify({ title }),
  });
  const conv = await res.json();
  setActiveConversationId(conv.id);
  triggerRefresh();
  return conv.id;
}, [triggerRefresh, sessionId]);
```

**API Endpoint:**
- **POST** `/api/conversations`
- Headers: `X-Session-ID` (user session)
- Body: `{ title: string }`
- Response: `{ id, title, created_at, updated_at, session_id }`

### Backend Conversation Creation
**File:** `/Users/cyyeh/Desktop/duckdb-data-agent/.claude/worktrees/implement-memory/backend/app/routes/conversations.py` (lines 31-38)

```python
@router.post("")
async def create_conversation(
    request: CreateConversationRequest,
